WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.060
Good morning, John.

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.780
today I want to do something a little different
that might not be appealing to everyone. I'm

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.640
going to make a video about making videos.
And of course, if you don't care about making

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.500
videos, I'm going to do my best to make it
entertaining nonetheless.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.900
Ok, first let's talk about what I'm not going
to do, I'm not going to talk about your equipment.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.940
I don't care what kind of camera you have!
I don't care what kind of computer you have

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.810
or what kind of software you have! This is
not about that! I believe that skill is honed

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.429
by lack, and there's no reason to have a sword
made of Valyrian steel if you're just learning

00:00:22.429 --> 00:00:25.269
how to wield a knife . So let us talk first
about what's actually important, which is

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:26.560
how to look and sound.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.339
Important Thing: The Rule of Thirds. Divide
your screen into thirds this way and this

00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:34.130
way. One of the interesting things about vlogging
is that early on both the eyes and the mouth

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:37.160
were falling on those lines, but now that
screens have gotten a little bit bigger, generally

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.080
it's just the eyes that are falling on the
line, because the eyesónot the mouthóactually

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.240
are the most important element of your frame!
I think that says something fundamental about

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.270
human nature. I'm just not sure what it is.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.950
Now, how you sound. Imagine for a moment me
going downstairs and talking to my wife the

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:52.910
way that I talk while I'm vlogging. That does
not happen! This is not my normal talking

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:57.080
voice. Surprise, surprise! The way that I
imagine it is that I am on a gigantic stage,

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.770
and there is one person in the audience, and
I'm talking to that one person, but I can't

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:01.460
talk to them like a normal person 'cause I'm
on a gigantic stage!

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.070
Now this is obviously a difficult thing to
hone; you're not going to get your vlogging

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:07.460
voice immediately. Watch early vlogbrothers
videos and see that we sucked too when we

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.649
started. It's nice for me that the one person
in the audience is generallyóor at least

00:01:10.649 --> 00:01:14.249
started out beingómy brother. So I knew how
to talk to my brother; I knew what would make

00:01:14.249 --> 00:01:18.020
him happy. Now that one person has changed,
and it's kind of an amalgam of all of Nerdfighteria.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:22.070
It's just each of you individually I'm trying
to imagine all at once; it's very strange.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:24.359
Now moving on, there's Don't Forget To Be
Awesome, which is one of the most important

00:01:24.359 --> 00:01:28.179
rules in life, but there's also, for vlogging,
another one: Don't Forget To Be Interesting.

00:01:28.179 --> 00:01:31.360
I even write out scripts sometimes, so that
I make sure that what I'm saying...isn't dull

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.929
as hell. I wrote a script for this video;
I'm going to post that script on my Tumblr

00:01:34.929 --> 00:01:38.069
so you can see the difference between the
script and what actually gets made into the

00:01:38.069 --> 00:01:39.069
video.

00:01:39.069 --> 00:01:40.999
Also never forget that even the best audience,
there will be parts of it that will have a

00:01:40.999 --> 00:01:43.909
very short attention span, and you will have
to pander to those people. But honestly, it's

00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:47.189
fun, and I truly believe that pandering to
those people actually makes your video better.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:50.170
There's a lot of ways to keep things interesting,
you could move around, put some video over

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:54.389
your voice. You could use props; awesome,
funny hats. Go outside! You can sing, you

00:01:54.389 --> 00:01:58.609
can sing songs. You can speed things up, or
you can slow things down. Use filters, and

00:01:58.609 --> 00:02:02.249
you can use puppets. A lot of times people
ask me how I get ideas for videos, but really

00:02:02.249 --> 00:02:05.079
it's not about having ideas for videos; that's
easy. Mostly I'm trying to figure out how

00:02:05.079 --> 00:02:06.579
to make those ideas interesting.

00:02:06.579 --> 00:02:11.510
Another very important rule: Silence...is
extremely powerful! Use it very sparingly.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.930
If you watch one of my videos you will notice
that there are very few moments that do not

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:18.730
have sound in them, and that is especially
true of the space around jumpcuts. Any silence

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.540
around a jumpcut is bad bad bad bad, BAD!

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:27.260
Another important rule: Do not be afraid...to
try! I know that failing at something stings

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:32.180
a lot less...if you didn't really try hard,
but, it's also much more likely.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.760
And finally, let's talk about editingóno
we're not going to do that because that would

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:41.510
take forever, so instead I am literally going
to post a screen capture of me editing this

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:42.632
vlog. I'm gonna put that on my second channel
at youtube.com/hankschannel, hankschannel!

00:02:42.632 --> 00:02:48.140
And you will be able to see how I made this
video, how I did all the tricks in this video,

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.750
and all the things that I do to make my videoblog
seem...professional, and crisp, and good,

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.020
and entertaining, and all of those things.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.180
So that's how you vlog! Of course, you can
do it however you want to do it, but I figured

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:00.290
people might be interested in seeing how I
do it. I encourage all of you to vlog, and

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.890
I encourage you to do it well. The video of
me editing this vlog might not be online as

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:07.220
soon as this goes up on the internet, but
it will be online shortly thereafter, and

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.209
there will be a link to it in the endscreen.

00:03:09.209 --> 00:03:10.459
John, I'll see you on Monday.

